**Offered:** Prior to 2025–26

### Course Description
Continuation of the first Real Analysis course. Focused on functions of several variables, metric spaces, and further topics in integration and differentiation in higher dimensions.

### Typical Syllabus
- Topology of \( \mathbb{R}^n \): open/closed sets, compactness, connectedness
- Multivariable functions: limits, continuity, differentiability
- Inverse and Implicit Function Theorems
- Integration in \( \mathbb{R}^n \): multiple integrals, change of variables
- Introduction to manifolds or differential forms (time permitting)

